            from measurable spaces to σ-complete Boolean algebras (where the morphisms are required to preserve countable unions and complements).
          %h3#from_complete_boolean_algebras_to_measurable_spaces From σ-complete Boolean algebras to measurable spaces
          %p
            Let
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi Σ
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \Sigma
            be a σ-complete Boolean algebra. We can define a
            %strong
              point of
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi Σ
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \Sigma
            to be any of the following equivalent structures:
          %ul
            %li
              A
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/zero-one+measure"} zero-one measure
              on
              = succeed "," do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi Σ
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \Sigma
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi p
                    %mo :
                    %mi Σ
                    %mo →
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} {
                    %mn 0
                    %mo ,
                    %mn 1
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} }
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} p:\Sigma\to\{0,1\}
              which is countably additive and for which
