          %h3#the_adjunction The adjunction
          %p
            Just as in the topological case, the functors
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi Σ
                  %mo :
                  %msup
                    %mi Meas
                    %mi op
                  %mo →
                  %mi σ
                  %mi Bool
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \Sigma: Meas^{op} \to \sigma Bool
            and
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi Sp
                  %mo :
                  %mi σ
                  %msup
                    %mi Bool
                    %mi op
                  %mo →
                  %mi Meas
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Sp: \sigma Bool^{op}\to Meas
            form a (contravariant)
            = succeed ":" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/idempotent+adjunction"} idempotent adjunction
          %ul
            %li
              The
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/unit+of+an+adjunction"} unit
              has as components measurable functions
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi η
                    %mo :
                    %mi X
                    %mo →
                    %mi Sp
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %msub
                      %mi Σ
                      %mi X
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \eta: X \to Sp(\Sigma_X)
              which map a point
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi x
                    %mo ∈
                    %mi X
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} x\in X
              to the corresponding
              %span.newWikiWord
                principal filter
                %a{:href => "/nlab/new/principal+filter"} ?
              on
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi Σ
                      %mi X
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \Sigma_X
              (or equivalently, to the
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Dirac+measure"} Dirac delta
              = succeed ")" do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/zero-one+measure"} zero-one measure
              = succeed ":" do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %msub
                        %mi δ
                        %mi x
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \delta_x
              = succeed "," do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi A
                      %mo ∈
                      %msub
                        %mi Σ
                        %mi X
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} A\in\Sigma_X
              .maruku-equation
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %msub
                        %mi δ
                        %mi x
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mi A
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %mo =
                      %mrow
                        %mo {
                        %mrow
                          %mtable{:columnalign => "left left", :displaystyle => "false"}
                            %mtr
                              %mtd
                                %mn 1
                              %mtd
                                %mi x
                                %mo ∈
                                %mi A
                            %mtr
                              %mtd
                                %mn 0
                              %mtd
                                %mi x
                                %mo ∉
                                %mi A
                                %mo .
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                      \\delta_x (A) = \begin{cases}
                      1 &amp; x\in A \\
                      0 &amp; x\notin A .
                      \\end{cases}
            %li
              The
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/counit"} counit
              has as components morphisms of
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi σ
                    %msup
                      %mi Bool
                      %mi op
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \sigma Bool^{op}
              in the form
              = succeed "," do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %msup
                        %mi ϵ
                        %mi op
                      %mo :
                      %msub
                        %mi Σ
                        %mrow
                          %mi Sp
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                          %mi Σ
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %mo →
                      %mi Σ
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \epsilon^{op}:\Sigma_{Sp(\Sigma)}\to\Sigma
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi σ
                    %mi Bool
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \sigma Bool
              of the form
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi ϵ
                    %mo :
                    %mi Σ
                    %mo →
                    %msub
                      %mi Σ
                      %mrow
                        %mi Sp
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                        %mi Σ
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \epsilon:\Sigma\to \Sigma_{Sp(\Sigma)}
              mapping
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi A
                    %mo ∈
                    %mi Σ
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} A\in\Sigma
              to the set
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msup
                      %mi A
                      %mo *
                    %mo ∈
                    %msub
                      %mi Σ
                      %mrow
                        %mi Sp
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                        %mi Σ
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} A^*\in\Sigma_{Sp(\Sigma)}
              defined above.
          %p
            The adjunction induces an
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/idempotent+monad"} idempotent monad
            on
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi Meas
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Meas
            (the
            = succeed ")," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/zero-one+measure#the_monad_of_zeroone_measures"} monad of zero-one measures
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi σ
                  %mi Bool
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \sigma Bool
            as well (or equivalently, an idempotent
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/comonad"} comonad
            on
            = succeed ")." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi σ
                    %msup
                      %mi Bool
                      %mi op
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \sigma Bool^{op}
          %p
            As usual with idempotent adjunctions, we have that the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/fixed+point+of+an+adjunction"} center
            is equivalently given by
          %ul
            %li
              The full subcategory of
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi Meas
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Meas
              whose objects are those spaces for which the unit
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi η
                    %mo :
                    %mi X
                    %mo →
                    %mi Sp
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %msub
                      %mi Σ
                      %mi X
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \eta:X\to Sp(\Sigma_X)
              is an isomorphism. These are sometimes called
              = succeed "." do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/sober+measurable+spaces"} sober measurable spaces
              = succeed "," do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/sober+topological+spaces"} sober topological spaces
            %li
              The full subcategory of
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi σ
                    %mi Bool
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \sigma Bool
              whose objects are those σ-algebras for which the counit
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi ϵ
                    %mo :
                    %mi Σ
                    %mo →
                    %msub
                      %mi Σ
                      %mrow
                        %mi Sp
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                        %mi Σ
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \epsilon:\Sigma\to \Sigma_{Sp(\Sigma)}
              is an isomorphism. These are sometimes called
              %strong spatial
              or
              %strong concrete
              σ-algebras.
          %p
            Because of this, sometimes one calls the monad on
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi Meas
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Meas
            the
            = succeed "." do
              %em sobrification monad
          %h2#particular_results Particular results
          %p (Work in progress. For now see the references.)
          %h3#equivalence_with_measurable_gelfand_duality Equivalence with measurable Gelfand duality
          %p
            (See at
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/measurable+Gelfand+duality#equivalence_with_loomissikorski_duality"} measurable Gelfand duality - Equivalence with Loomis-Sikorski duality
            = succeed ".)" do
              %a{:href => "#fritz_lorenzin"} FL’25, Section 4.1
